From 2c2d31d0b115e27d85f05c0c914bca3b5295298c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mirko Brombin <9479903+mirkobrombin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 19:57:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] mm: fault anonymous pages through SWP_MTS objects

Reserve a native software-leaf type and convert eligible single-mapped base anonymous folios through migration entries before provider I/O. The immediate TLB flush freezes writers before the immutable payload is checksummed and stored.

Install generation-backed SWP_MTS PTEs, duplicate exact object references across fork, release them on zap, and promote through the anonymous major-fault path without legacy swap ownership. Provider and fault references prevent slot reuse during I/O.

Keep the first reclaim path deliberately narrow: large or multiply mapped resident folios fall back instead of risking partial conversion. Nonresident objects may become shared after fork and retain lazy COW semantics.

Evidence: Linux 7.1.3 CONFIG_MTS_TIER=y make -j4 mm/; checkpatch.pl --strict (clean).
Signed-off-by: Mirko Brombin <9479903+mirkobrombin@users.noreply.github.com>
